# moment kind=street3d cam=worm near=1.1 traffic=34 art="GUESS|one full day in Vietnam" artfx=stack artAt=-0.25 artOut=5.6 dur=6.5 fg=wires trans=cut
Guess what one full day in Vietnam costs.
Breakfast. Coffee. A ride.
Two meals, a beer… and a bed.
# talk place=oldquarter host=linh pose=present big="8 PRICES" shots="WS|MS|CU" dur=8.5 trans=cut
Eight real prices, all checked this month.
Then the total.
And one thing that quietly costs four times what it should.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=banhmi hold=banhmi item="bánh mì" vnd="25.000 ₫" usd="$1" checked="Oct 2026" react=yummy art="25.000 ₫|breakfast" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=7 trans=whip
Breakfast first. A bánh mì from a cart: *twenty-five thousand dong*.
That's about [one dollar].
# countdown n=2 text="Cà phê đen đá" sub="20.000 ₫ · ≈ $0.80" prop=caphe size=1.6 bg=#17224d capY=.6 dur=6 trans=iris
Iced black coffee at a street café: *twenty thousand*.
Strong enough to reset your morning.
# price place=oldquarter hero=dave seller=xeom item="GrabBike ride" vnd="30.000 ₫" usd="$1.15" checked="Oct 2026" art="30.000 ₫|GrabBike across town" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=7 trans=whip
Crossing town by GrabBike: *thirty thousand*.
Cheaper than the walk is long.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=cophovn hold=pho item="phở bò" vnd="45.000 ₫" usd="$1.80" checked="Oct 2026" react=yummy art="45.000 ₫|lunch" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="MS|CU" dur=7 trans=circles
Lunch: a bowl of phở, *forty-five thousand*.
Most of Hà Nội eats this before midday.
# stat value=120000 from=0 suffix=" ₫" label="spent before noon · about $4.60" bg=#17224d dur=5.5 trans=ink
So by noon you've spent a hundred and twenty thousand.
About four dollars sixty.
# countdown n=5 text="Museum ticket" sub="40.000 ₫ · ≈ $1.55" prop=ticket size=1.6 bg=#17224d capY=.8 dur=5 trans=whip
Afternoon. A museum ticket: *forty thousand*.
# social place=night_market hero=dave host=xeom toasts=2 cheer="MỘT, HAI, BA… DZÔ!" fg=lanterns shots="MS|CU" dur=8 trans=tear art="10.000 ₫|a glass of bia hơi" artfx=count artAt=1.8
Evening. Bia hơi, brewed this morning: *ten thousand* a glass.
Two glasses, and you're still under half a dollar.
# price place=sidewalk hero=dave seller=cophovn hold=buncha item="bún chả" vnd="55.000 ₫" usd="$2.10" checked="Oct 2026" react=happy art="55.000 ₫|dinner" artfx=count artAt=1.4 shots="CU|MS" dur=7 trans=fgwipe
Dinner. Bún chả, grilled over coals: *fifty-five thousand*.
# dialogue a=dave b=hostel place=oldquarter voiceA=am_puck voiceB=am_fenrir act="hostel:point" lines="a:thinking:And a bed for tonight?|b:happy:Dorm. Two hundred thousand.|a:shocked:…Eight dollars?|b:smug:With breakfast."
# budget title="ONE DAY IN VIETNAM" items="Bánh mì;25k|Coffee;20k|GrabBike;30k|Phở;45k|Museum;40k|Bia hơi ×2;20k|Bún chả;55k|Dorm bed;200k" total="435.000 ₫" usd="≈ $17" checked="Oct 2026" dur=11.5 drop=1.0 art="435.000 ₫|a whole day · ≈ $17" artfx=slam artAt=1.2 trans=cut
Eight things. One full day.
Four hundred and thirty-five thousand dong.
[About seventeen dollars.]
# moment kind=pass hero=dave place=hagiang time=sunset capY=.52 dur=8.5 art="155.000 ₫|a bed in Hà Giang · dinner included" artfx=count artAt=1.6 trans=cut
And that's a city price.
Up in Hà Giang, a homestay bed is about *a hundred and fifty-five thousand*.
Dinner usually comes with it.
# compare leftTitle="STREET CAFÉ" rightTitle="TOURIST CAFÉ" left=barista right=dave leftPrice="20.000 ₫;$0.80;cà phê đen đá" rightPrice="90.000 ₫;$3.50;same coffee, nicer chair" checked="Oct 2026" capY=.56 shots="WS|CU" dur=9 trans=inkbleed
Now the thing nobody warns you about.
The same iced coffee, fifty metres away: *ninety thousand*.
Four times the price. For the chair.
# steps place=oldquarter title="DON'T OVERPAY" items="Eat where the stools are full|Agree the price before you get on|Book the ride in the app, not at the kerb" icons="banhmi|money|phone" host=linh capY=.52 shots="MS|CU" dur=10 trans=cut
Three rules. Eat where the plastic stools are already full.
Agree a price before you get on anything.
And book the ride in the app, not at the kerb.
